SUMMARY:CenterFest Arts Festival
DESCRIPTION:Since 1975\, CenterFest has brought Durham together through art\, music\, food\, and community. North Carolina’s longest-running outdoor juried arts festival returns to downtown Durham September\n19–20\, 2026\, welcoming thousands of visitors to celebrate the creativity that makes Durham unique. \nThis year’s festival highlights Durham Arts Council’s “Culture\nLives Here” initiative as part of America’s 250th anniversary\ncelebration. At the heart of the story is the DAC Building\, originally built in 1906 as Durham High School and later serving as Durham City Hall. For generations\, it has stood as a symbol of learning\, civic engagement\, and creativity. \nJoin the Durham Arts Council on September 19–20 and take home a piece of Durham history with the commemorative design celebrating the creative spirit that continues to thrive in our city! Find out more information here.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/centerfest-arts-festival/
LOCATION:Downtown Durham\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
END:VEVENT
